{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3108","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3108","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3108\",\"parent_revision\":\"35608af4eaf7ed2d663da2a9a20ab8c47fcdf9e0\",\"root_revision\":\"d5fb2156065b062c5ab8953cb12c707c6fa7ec581742ded73e180382146180d7\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: Ideas\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-21\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nThis is an exploration/experiment item \u2014 its deliverable is an experiment result or design decision with evidence (a prototype on a real plan, a measured comparison, or a written design verdict), not a mandate to ship a feature.\\n\\nOrigin: mechanism mined from Claude Code's built-in ultracode Workflow orchestration system \u2014 a code-executed multi-agent workflow runtime whose design contract contains several simple-but-effective patterns DH can adopt without adopting the runtime itself.\\n\\nShared design constraint (same as #3097\u2013#3103): the model keeps the judgment but writes it down once, as typed data, at planning time; the mechanical consequence is applied deterministically by machinery that already exists. No new scheduler, no generic graph runtime \u2014 out of scope.\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **explore loop-until-dry convergence criteria for discovery and audit sweeps** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: ultracode Workflow orchestration system\\n- **Priority**: Ideas\\n- **Added**: 2026-08-21\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## What Why\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z-0</sub>\\n\\nBorrowed from ultracode: for unknown-size discovery (bugs, issues, edge cases, affected files), keep spawning finders until K consecutive rounds return nothing new \u2014 \\\"simple counters (while count < N) miss the tail.\\\" And its hard-won convergence detail: deduplicate new findings against everything SEEN, not against confirmed findings, otherwise verifier-rejected findings reappear every round and the loop never converges. DH's discovery-shaped work (grooming research, impact-radius inventory, doc-drift audits, review sweeps) currently uses either fixed-size passes (one agent, one sweep) or unbounded judgment (\\\"keep looking until done\\\"), with no data-defined stopping rule \u2014 so sweeps either under-cover (miss the tail) or over-run (no convergence signal).\\n</div>\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z-1</sub>\\n\\nBorrowed from ultracode: for unknown-size discovery (bugs, issues, edge cases, affected files), keep spawning finders until K consecutive rounds return nothing new \u2014 \\\"simple counters (while count < N) miss the tail.\\\" And its hard-won convergence detail: deduplicate new findings against everything SEEN, not against confirmed findings, otherwise verifier-rejected findings reappear every round and the loop never converges. DH's discovery-shaped work (grooming research, impact-radius inventory, doc-drift audits, review sweeps) currently uses either fixed-size passes (one agent, one sweep) or unbounded judgment (\\\"keep looking until done\\\"), with no data-defined stopping rule \u2014 so sweeps either under-cover (miss the tail) or over-run (no convergence signal).\\n</div>\\n\\n## Mitigates\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nUnder-coverage from fixed single-pass sweeps; unbounded spend from sweeps with no stopping rule; non-convergence from deduplicating against the wrong set.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Benefit Lands In\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z-0</sub>\\n\\nGrooming (impact-radius and research completeness), audit skills (doc-drift, dead-code), and review sweeps \u2014 anywhere the result-set size is unknown upfront.\\n</div>\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z-1</sub>\\n\\nGrooming (impact-radius and research completeness), audit skills (doc-drift, dead-code), and review sweeps \u2014 anywhere the result-set size is unknown upfront.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Proposed Exploration\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z-0</sub>\\n\\n1. Identify the DH steps that are discovery-shaped (unknown result-set size) vs transform-shaped (known inputs) \u2014 only the former get the pattern.\\n2. Define the convergence rule as data: K (consecutive dry rounds to stop, likely 2) and the seen-set identity key per finding type.\\n3. Prototype on ONE discovery step (impact-radius inventory during grooming is the best candidate \u2014 its completeness directly gates planning quality) and compare coverage and cost against the current single-pass baseline.\\n4. Record the seen-vs-confirmed dedup rule in the step's instructions explicitly.\\n</div>\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z-1</sub>\\n\\n1. Identify the DH steps that are discovery-shaped (unknown result-set size) vs transform-shaped (known inputs) \u2014 only the former get the pattern.\\n2. Define the convergence rule as data: K (consecutive dry rounds to stop, likely 2) and the seen-set identity key per finding type.\\n3. Prototype on ONE discovery step (impact-radius inventory during grooming is the best candidate \u2014 its completeness directly gates planning quality) and compare coverage and cost against the current single-pass baseline.\\n4. Record the seen-vs-confirmed dedup rule in the step's instructions explicitly.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Related\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n#3102 (the round counter is the same counters-as-data mechanism); #3097 (round sizing can key off complexity).\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"0843b4e070007638ed76b5c2e199ae9b0968d67777f02dd01dd261521faa9d49\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABQIqRdA\"}"}